WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.540
The output of AI-assisted documentation should be reusable, not just readable.

2
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:21.000
Common outputs include an attack surface register, system summary, component table, data flow summary, interface inventory, identity and permission summary, dependency map, risk notes, open questions, and review checklist.

3
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.860
Each output serves a different audience and decision.

4
00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.580
An attack surface register is often the central artifact.

5
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:43.320
It can list components, interfaces, exposure level, data types, identities, owners, dependencies, trust boundaries, assumptions, evidence links, open questions, and review status.

6
00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.900
The register does not need to be fancy.

7
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.280
It needs to be structured enough that teams can filter, update, and review it over time.

8
00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:55.560
A system summary helps new reviewers understand the big picture.

9
00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:00.060
A component table helps developers and architects confirm the system inventory.

10
00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:06.080
A data flow summary supports privacy review, threat modeling, and incident response.

11
00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:11.380
An identity and permission summary helps security teams evaluate access patterns.

12
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:16.200
Risk notes connect the documentation to decisions and follow-up work.

13
00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.400
Open questions are not a weakness.

14
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.580
They are one of the most valuable outputs because they make uncertainty actionable.

15
00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:32.440
If an owner is missing, a data type is unknown, a third-party integration is unclear, or a logging assumption is unverified, the document should say so.

16
00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:35.420
Hidden uncertainty creates false confidence.

17
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:39.380
Reusable outputs work best when they are easy to maintain.

18
00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:46.120
Use stable identifiers, clear field names, source references, ownership fields, and review status.

19
00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:57.420
AI can help generate first drafts and updates, but the structure should be designed for ongoing use by developers, security teams, architects, auditors, and incident responders.
